# PMPSeg

PMPSeg is a processed B-Rep CAD dataset for face-level machining process decision-making of prismatic parts. It supports three manufacturing prediction tasks:

1. initial-setup/clamping-face prediction;
2. machining-strategy prediction;
3. tool-direction prediction.

Each CAD face has aligned labels for the three tasks. The dataset contains processed B-Rep data files, raw label files, and official dataset split information.

## Download

The full PMPSeg dataset is publicly available as a versioned GitHub release:

https://github.com/niushuai7911359/PMPSeg/releases/tag/v1.0

Please download `PMPSeg.rar` from the **Assets** section of the release page.

## Directory structure

```text
PMPSeg/
├── initialsetup faceLabel/     # initial-setup/clamping labels
├── MachiningStrategyLabel/     # machining-strategy labels
├── toolDirectionLabel/         # tool-direction labels
├── processed/                  # processed B-Rep data and labels
│   └── dataset.json            # train/validation/test split lists
└── README.md
```

Files belonging to the same CAD model share the same numeric stem. For example:

```text
initialsetup faceLabel/00001.txt
MachiningStrategyLabel/00001.seg
toolDirectionLabel/00001.txt
processed/00001.npz
```

## Dataset splits

The file `processed/dataset.json` provides the official `training_set`, `validation_set`, and `test_set` splits. Please use these official splits when reporting comparable experimental results.

## Notes

The released dataset is intended for academic research on B-Rep-based machining process decision-making, including machining strategy prediction, machining direction prediction, and initial setup face prediction.

## Acknowledgement

The B-Rep data processing and topology extraction in PMPSeg are based on [Open CASCADE Technology (OCCT)](https://dev.opencascade.org/).
